communications.communication:
The records produced in response to my request appear to be incomplete.

I have video evidence showing uniformed Oakland Police Department officers approaching a street vendor on Monday, May 1, 2026, and destroying the vendor’s water cooler in a trash compactor. The officers appear to be standing next to other City personnel, including individuals identified as “Civilian Technician.”

The incident occurred during street-vendor enforcement activity in Fruitvale and/or Downtown Oakland and appears to have been part of a multi-department operation involving street vendors.

Please provide all records concerning this May 1, 2026 incident, including but not limited to:

1. Body-worn camera footage;
2. Incident reports, CAD logs, dispatch records, notes, and call histories;
3. Emails, text messages, Teams/Slack messages, memoranda, or other communications concerning the incident;
4. Records identifying the officers and City employees present;
5. Records identifying the “Civilian Technician” personnel present;
6. Records concerning the destruction, seizure, disposal, or handling of the vendor’s water cooler or other property;
7. Records concerning any planned or coordinated street-vendor enforcement operation in Fruitvale or Downtown Oakland on May 1, 2026;
8. Records involving OPD, civilian technicians, Public Works, Code Enforcement, Economic and Workforce Development, or any other City department involved in the operation; and
9. Any photographs, videos, reports, after-action summaries, or internal communications related to the incident.

Please also conduct a supplemental search and identify which departments, custodians, and search terms were used. If any responsive records are withheld, please identify the specific exemption claimed and provide all reasonably segregable non-exempt portions.

Thank you.
